PROGRAM 12: 
Write a shell script to monitor process activities. 
a. Display all running processes. b. Display processes belonging to the current user. c. Show top five CPU consuming processes. d. Display process ID and parent process ID. e. Display the total number of running processes.
echo "Display all running process"
ps -e
echo "Display process belonging to the current user" 
ps -u $(whoami) 
echo "Show top five CPU consuming process"
ps -eo pid,comm,%cpu-sort=-%cpu|head -6 
echo "Display process ID and parent process ID" 
ps -eo pid,ppid,comm 
echo "Display the total number of running process"
ps -e h |wc -l 
